  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start ready Pakistan - National Reserve Fund Project Khairpur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Fund localization Hub Pakistan started Disaster Risk Funding (DRF) in Pakistan for preparedeness and response floods, heatwave and drought models. The contigency plans are developed before the emergency situation which reviewed by national Steering Committee and presented to Start Fund governing body. HelpAge Pakistan office submitted four proposals for anticipatory response in Sindh and Punjab. The rain floods started in June 2022 and NSC decided to utilize national reserves for activities segregated as 30% for preparedeness and 70% for response. Start Fund and National Steering Committee approved funds for one location &apos;District Khairpur&quot; from National Reserve Funds of GBP21,544.</narrative>
  </description>
